=== CRITERION 4 — over-pinning report (observations, not failures) ===

What the three blocks pin, exactly:
  - Blocks A and C (four regions) pin ONLY `role="region" aria-label="X">`.
    They pin nothing else — no class, no tabindex, no table markup.
  - Block B (Deleted) pins the FULL wrapper string
    `<div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Deleted major expense definitions">`
    — i.e. class list AND attribute ORDER — plus
    `class="text-body-sm px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-positive` and the
    page-wide absence of `text-xs px-2 py-0.5`.

O1 (UNDER-pinning, the more interesting direction): removing `tabindex="0"` from
   the four NON-Deleted regions leaves the suite GREEN. Verified: mutation M9
   stripped tabindex from the "Unmatched exceptions", "Unmatched exceptions over
   threshold", "New merchant exceptions" and "Matched but anomalous amount table"
   wrappers (grep confirmed 1 remaining `tabindex="0" role="region"`, the Deleted
   one) and `go test -count=1` reported `ok budget2/internal/templates 0.044s`.
   `overflow-x-auto` is likewise unpinned on those four. Keyboard focusability —
   the actual axe `scrollable-region-focusable` defect BL1 fixed — is therefore
   guarded for one of five regions. The BL5 contract only asks for the region
   LABELS there ("renders inside aria-label=…"), so this is in-contract; flagging
   it as a cheap hardening for the backlog (pin the full wrapper string in all
   five, as block B already does).

O2 (OVER-pinning, mild): block B's positive button clause includes the unrelated
   styling classes `rounded border border-positive`, so a pure restyle of the
   Restore button's border colour would fail a target-size guard. Similarly the
   wrapper assertion is order-sensitive: reordering attributes to an equivalent
   `role="region" tabindex="0" …` would fail. Both are brittleness, not
   incorrectness.

O3 (scope of the negative clause): `strings.Contains(html, "text-xs px-2 py-0.5")`
   is asserted over the WHOLE rendered page, not the Deleted panel. Measured
   today that is precise — `grep -c 'text-xs px-2 py-0\.5'` = 2 on master's
   major-expenses.html (the two buttons), 0 on BL1's, and the only other repo
   occurrence is components/whatif/healthcare-person.html:16, not rendered by
   `major-expenses-content`. A future unrelated small badge on this page would
   trip it spuriously.

